{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ADHD\n\nCondition hub: ADHD heterogeneity, competing cognitive accounts, rater-dependent measurement, and the shape of the treatment evidence.\n\n[[ADHD Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-27; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1800,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD across the lifespan]]**\n*condition* - 7 sources\n\nLifespan presentation, heterogeneity and measurement sources in ADHD, with function distinguished from symptom counts.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Heterogeneity and presentations in ADHD]]**\n*framework* - 8 sources\n\nWhy ADHD is better described as a heterogeneous set of profiles than as one deficit, with consequences for measurement and treatment.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD diagnosis and measurement]]**\n*method* - 10 sources\n\nMulti-source assessment, rater and task measurement problems, and the adult-specific limits of retrospective reporting in ADHD.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Rater and measurement effects in ADHD]]**\n*method* - 9 sources\n\nHow parent, teacher, clinician and self-report measures of ADHD diverge, and why that is measurement rather than noise.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1146,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD in girls and women]]**\n*condition* - 5 sources\n\nHow ADHD presents and is recognised in girls and women: the shifting sex ratio, later diagnosis after internalising diagnoses, small instrument-dependent presentation differences, hormonal influences, and what the evidence does not show.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1384,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Constructs and assessment",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1364
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD and prefrontal catecholamines]]**\n*mechanism* - 5 sources\n\nHow prefrontal dopamine and noradrenaline modulate attention, why the relationship is an inverted U, and what the evidence does and does not license.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Reinforcement learning accounts of ADHD]]**\n*theory* - 9 sources\n\nAccounts that explain ADHD-related behaviour through altered reinforcement sensitivity or learning rate, and their evidence.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Cognitive models of ADHD]]**\n*theory* - 8 sources\n\nThe main cognitive accounts of ADHD - executive function, the dual pathway with delay aversion, state regulation and default-mode interference - and what the evidence for each does and does not show.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 908,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Accounts",
			"x": 460,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 864
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD medication evidence]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nShort-term randomised evidence, rater and dose effects, tolerability patterns, and the long-term evidence gap in ADHD medication research.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[CBT for adult ADHD]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nWhat CBT for adult ADHD targets, why comparator and rater determine the result, and how it sits in the wider adult intervention evidence.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Short-term versus long-term outcomes]]**\n*method* - 9 sources\n\nHow the evidence horizon bounds a treatment claim, what remains open at 26 and 52 weeks, and the certainty tools used to say so.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD and substance use]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nHow far childhood ADHD predicts later substance use disorders, and what between-person, within-person and emulated-trial evidence says about ADHD medication and later substance problems.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 1146,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
